Package: journal-maker
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 pandoc (>= 3.0),
 texlive-xetex,
 texlive-latex-recommended,
 texlive-fonts-recommended,
 lmodern,
 poppler-utils,
 qpdf,
 citation-style-language-styles,
Description: build a Google-Scholar-indexable static journal from Markdown
 Turns per-article Markdown plus TOML bibliographic metadata into a fully
 static academic journal website: one HTML landing page per article carrying
 Highwire Press citation_* meta tags and a visible abstract, a camera-ready
 PDF built via pandoc and XeLaTeX in the same directory (as Google Scholar
 requires), a homepage, per-volume browse pages, sitemap.xml and robots.txt.
 References are cited by stable @key from a per-article BibTeX bibliography
 and numbered by pandoc citeproc (IEEE style, numbered by first appearance),
 so inserting a reference never renumbers the body.
 Ships a Scholar-compliance checker that fails the build on any violation
 (missing required meta, oversized or non-searchable PDF, mislocated
 citation_pdf_url, dangling or uncited reference, leftover wiki markup) and a
 de-wiki drafting aid that turns MediaWiki source into a Markdown starting
 point. No server-side logic at serve time; deterministic and reproducible.
